---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CalculatorsList from '../components/CalculatorsList.astro';
---

<Layout>
	<h1>Sanjay Srikanth</h1>
		<section class="bio">
		<p>
		I am a <span id="age"></span>-year-old software engineer working in the spaceflight industry, based in Santa Barbara, California, United States.
		</p>
		<p>
		I grew up in Santa Clarita, a suburb north of Los Angeles. I attended <a href="https://www.sauguscenturions.com/">Saugus High School</a> in
		Santa Clarita from 2018 to 2022, graduating as salutatorian with a 4.79 GPA and 1520 SAT score (800 math, 720 English). I  
		attended <a href="https://www.ucsb.edu/">UC Santa Barbara</a> from 2022 to 2026, majoring in computer science, where I was a regents
		and honors scholar, participated in the <a href="https://ersp.cs.ucsb.edu/">Early Research Scholars Program</a> during my 3rd year, 
		and graduated with a 3.64 GPA. I currently work as a software engineer for Santa Barbara-based 
		company <a href="https://umbra.space/">Umbra Space</a>, which manufactures satellites that use synthetic aperture radar to image the Earth 
		at high resolution.
		</p>
		<p>
		In addition to software and aerospace, I am interested in geography, physics, math, and astronomy. I like making maps - I drafted a
		congressional district map of California following the 2020 census, and have made several maps of the world and the United States using QGIS
		and Inkscape, including demographic, electoral, weather/climate, and topographic maps, many of which are showcased on my Wikipedia user page
		(see Links below). Outside of work, I enjoy running, playing soccer, and playing video games like Minecraft. I am a big sports fan, particularly 
		in soccer and basketball.
		</p>
		</section>
